{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The smart plug feels like a useful next step because it would let me control a lamp with the Alexa devices I already use.",
    "The indoor camera connects with my earlier interest in home security, and wireless headphones could serve a practical need in my computer setup, although neither is an immediate purchase."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The older Echo Show, Echo Dot and Fire TV sticks duplicate devices I recently bought, so their familiarity does not give me a reason to choose them.",
    "I have no clear need for a tablet or AirPods right now. Owning Mac accessories and other electronics does not mean I need those devices.",
    "The three-camera pack and speaker-and-bulb bundle go beyond what I currently want to try; one camera or a smart plug would be a more useful starting point."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My Alexa purchases seem to be taken as a reason to suggest more Alexa speakers and displays, even when I already have newer versions.",
    "My history of buying computer accessories seems to be treated as broad interest in personal electronics, without a specific task those purchases would help me accomplish."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent purchases establish what I already have: a fourth-generation Dot, second-generation Show 5 and Fire TV Stick 4K Max make older alternatives less useful.",
    "The recent Show stand and my earlier replacement batteries suggest that I also look for ways to support and keep using existing equipment.",
    "Interest does not always mean I am ready to buy: I would wait for a need before choosing headphones and start with one camera before considering three."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The suggestions recognize my Alexa and practical electronics interests, but miss that I currently value useful additions to equipment I own more than duplicate devices."
}"}
